# Prevents core.autocrlf on some future checkout from rewriting LF to CRLF in served static assets --
# harmless for most files here, but this repo now also carries files that get hashed/compared byte-for-byte
# in other parts of the TourGuid estate (see TourGuid-App's own .gitattributes for the version of this
# problem that actually bit something). Cheap to apply broadly rather than re-discover per file later.
public/** text eol=lf

# ...but never for what is not text. `text` on a PNG makes git rewrite the CRLF bytes inside it (its own signature
# has one) when the file is added, so an innocent `git add` would commit a corrupted image. Later lines win.
public/**/*.png binary
public/**/*.jpg binary
public/**/*.jpeg binary
public/**/*.webp binary
public/**/*.gif binary
public/**/*.ico binary
public/**/*.woff binary
public/**/*.woff2 binary
public/**/*.mp4 binary
public/**/*.pdf binary
